  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "bassline (the Sheffield sound): four on the floor at 135-140 under a busy, bouncing sixteenth bass riff that is the lead, a clap on two and four and shuffled hats",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar: the riff moves in sixteenths and eighths between the root, the steps either side of it and the fourth, accented against the kick — the bass is the tune in this style. A clap on two and four, closed hats swung. The organ stab that usually answers it is not asked: the organ is declared not struck, so a short chop cannot reach it."
  }
